# Required. Use a fine-grained PAT restricted to TARGET_REPO with only:
# contents:write, pull-requests:write, and issues:write.
GITHUB_TOKEN=
META_API_KEY=
TARGET_REPO=owner/repository

# Optional operator settings.
# DATA_DIR defaults to ~/.simple-coding-agent/ and CLONE_DIR to $DATA_DIR/repo/.
# DATA_DIR=/path/to/agent-data
# CLONE_DIR=/path/to/persistent-clone
# POLL_INTERVAL=60
# LOG_LEVEL=INFO
# MODEL_TIMEOUT=3600
# PUBLISH_TIMEOUT=120
# MAX_RETRIES=3
# MAX_CONSECUTIVE_ERRORS=3

# Automatic continuation of handoff releases. With the default 0, continuing
# a `round-finished` issue always needs a human decision (re-applying
# `ready-for-agent`). With MAX_AUTO_CONTINUATIONS=N, the agent picks up a
# `round-finished` issue on its own, ahead of new `ready-for-agent` work, up
# to N automatic continuations in a row; a human requeue resets the count and
# grants another N rounds, and removing `round-finished` stops the sequence
# at any time. Operator-only: the repository profile refuses this key, so an
# agent-written PR can never raise its own round limit. See
# docs/adr/0005-automatic-continuation-budget.md.
# MAX_AUTO_CONTINUATIONS=0

# Handoff comment mode. With the default `link`, the first handoff creates one
# short shared comment per issue and later routine handoffs update its hidden
# record without posting an individual result comment or copying the note body
# into GitHub; the visible branch link keeps showing the latest note. Set
# `verbose` to keep the historical per-attempt handoff result comments
# (including the note body) for troubleshooting. Both modes share the same
# bookkeeping and recovery, still post explicit notifications when human
# action is needed, and leave existing comments untouched when switching.
# Operator-only: the repository profile refuses this key.
# HANDOFF_COMMENT_MODE=link

# Conflict requeue of published pull requests that report merge conflicts.
# With the default 0, a `merge-conflict` label is not part of the queue,
# no pull-request query runs, and a labelled issue waits untouched. With
# MAX_CONFLICT_ATTEMPTS above 0, workers detect conflicts on their own:
# every poll reads the repository's open pull requests in one paged query
# and labels an otherwise ordinary issue `merge-conflict` when its
# `agent/issue-N` branch reports `CONFLICTING`, so it is eligible in that
# same poll (a human may also apply the label manually). A `merge-conflict`
# issue meeting the base queue rules is claimed before automatic
# continuations and ordinary work; the conflict attempt rebases
# the published branch onto the base, runs setup plus one profile check,
# and force-pushes only when green, with no model call. N consecutive
# failed conflict attempts on one issue (a push that changes nothing counts)
# escalate instead of requeueing: the attempt whose failure reaches the
# budget adds `ready-for-human` and carries the handoff in its own result
# comment (`k/N`, the failure tail, a pull-request link). The agent never
# removes that label; a human hands the issue back by removing it, which
# requeues with the full budget. An issue carrying `ready-for-human` is
# neither labelled by the detector nor claimed from `merge-conflict`.
# Operator-only: the repository profile refuses this key, so an
# agent-written PR can never raise its own conflict budget. See
# docs/adr/0007-conflict-attempt-budget.md.
# MAX_CONFLICT_ATTEMPTS=0

# Shared-login worker pool. With the default (unset), this worker claims by
# GitHub login alone. To run several workers on one GitHub login, give each
# worker its own container and DATA_DIR plus a distinct WORKER_ID: a claimant
# is then a (login, worker id) pair, marked with a `claimed-by:<worker-id>`
# label that tells pool workers apart (created automatically when missing).
# WORKER_ID must use [a-z0-9-], at most 32 characters (the marker label
# limit is 50); anything else fails at startup. Release removes the worker's
# own marker first and the shared assignment only when no marker remains, so
# a yielding worker never strands the winner's claim, and an issue carrying
# any `claimed-by:*` label is never eligible. A lost /data directory or a
# changed WORKER_ID leaves the marker and assignment for a human: remove the
# stale `claimed-by:<old-id>` label (and the assignment, if the issue should
# requeue) by hand; there is no startup sweep and no TTL.
# WORKER_ID=worker-1

# Repository profile commands (setup/check) run with a deliberately minimal
# PATH (os.defpath) that excludes the orchestrator's own environment. If a
# profile command needs a tool installed outside that default PATH (e.g. `uv`
# under Homebrew at /opt/homebrew/bin, or ~/.local/bin), list its directories
# here, colon-separated. They are prepended to the command's PATH.
# PROFILE_EXTRA_PATH=/opt/homebrew/bin:/usr/local/bin

# By default the repository profile is read from
# docs/agents/simple-coding-agent-profile.yml inside the target repository.
# Set PROFILE_PATH to load it from elsewhere instead, e.g. alongside this
# agent's own Dockerfile/config.
# PROFILE_PATH=/path/to/simple-coding-agent-profile.yml

# The default false loads user-installed skills/settings only. Setting true also
# loads target-repository project settings. Hooks are disabled, but repository
# apiKeyHelper, settings env entries, and project-skill allowed-tools remain an
# accepted residual exposure. Enable it only for repositories you trust.
# AGENT_TRUST_PROJECT_SETTINGS=false

# By default, must-fix review findings block publication. An explicitly empty
# value selects the agreed test-only review gate.
# REVIEW_BLOCKING_SEVERITIES=must-fix

# When true, the orchestrator asks GitHub to merge the pull request it opens
# for a complete implementation, right after creating it: it first enables
# GitHub's native auto-merge with PR_MERGE_METHOD, so GitHub merges once the
# base branch's protection rules are met, and merges directly when GitHub
# refuses because the PR is already mergeable. A merge failure never changes
# a complete outcome; it is only reported in the issue result comment.
# Set PR_AUTO_MERGE=label instead to merge only issues explicitly opted in
# with the `agent-auto-merge` label: only collaborators with write access may
# apply it, and it counts only when the issue carried it at claim time, so a
# label added while an attempt runs (or after it finishes) never enables that
# attempt's merge. An unopted complete implementation still gets its PR; the
# result comment reports that auto-merge was skipped for lack of opt-in.
# WARNING: auto-merged PRs land on the base branch with no human review
# unless branch protection requires one (required checks and/or required
# reviews). See docs/agents/operator-onboarding.md and
# docs/adr/0004-pr-auto-merge-operator-setting.md before enabling.
# PR_AUTO_MERGE=false
# PR_MERGE_METHOD selects the merge method for both paths.
# PR_MERGE_METHOD=merge

# Token budget and handoff reserve. Each attempt counts every processed and
# generated token (unweighted, subagents included) against MAX_BUDGET_TOKENS
# (default 4000000); reaching it stops the attempt unconditionally (hard
# ceiling). Before that, the agent asks the model to hand off cooperatively
# once the soft threshold is crossed; the crossing latches for the attempt
# and is evaluated on every counted response and in the PreToolUse hook.
# The effective soft threshold is the earlier of two rules, computed from
# the main thread's latest context size:
#   soft = min(MAX_BUDGET_TOKENS * (1 - SOFT_THRESHOLD_PERCENTAGE),
#              MAX_BUDGET_TOKENS - (HANDOFF_RESERVE_TURNS + 1) * main_context_tokens)
# SOFT_THRESHOLD_PERCENTAGE (0-1, exclusive; default 0.2) sets the fixed
# share of the budget, and HANDOFF_RESERVE_TURNS (integer 1-20; default 6)
# guarantees that many turns after the crossing turn at the current context
# size. A huge context whose reserve exceeds the remaining budget trips the
# threshold on the next check. MAX_TURNS bounds turns per attempt.
# MAX_BUDGET_USD (default 20) is only a looser SDK circuit breaker, not
# authoritative Meta billing, with a startup floor check against the token
# budget at the $5/MTok reference rate. Turns/MODEL_TIMEOUT have no soft
# threshold; reaching either gets one best-effort handoff follow-up instead.
# See docs/agents/operator-onboarding.md.
# MAX_TURNS=60
# MAX_BUDGET_TOKENS=4000000
# SOFT_THRESHOLD_PERCENTAGE=0.2
# HANDOFF_RESERVE_TURNS=6
# MAX_BUDGET_USD=20
#
# MODEL_NAME pins the Meta model with no fallback. CLAUDE_CODE_VERSION no longer has any effect:
# the CLI version follows the pinned SDK release and its bundled CLI.
# MODEL_NAME=muse-spark-1.3-contributor
#
# The SDK pin lives in the project, not in this file: pyproject.toml pins
# claude-agent-sdk (the Dockerfile installs from it), and provenance
# verification checks the installed SDK against that pin, read from the
# installed package metadata. An upgrade changes only the pin (then run
# `uv lock`). CLAUDE_AGENT_SDK_VERSION set anywhere is ignored, including a
# value inherited from an SDK-hosted shell.

# Model backend settings. Defaults reproduce the current Meta behaviour, so an
# existing .env with only META_API_KEY keeps working with no edits.
# MODEL_BASE_URL=https://api.meta.ai
# MODEL_AUTH_MODE=auth_token
# MODEL_API_KEY falls back to META_API_KEY when unset; when both are set,
# MODEL_API_KEY wins. One of the two must be set.
# MODEL_API_KEY=
# MODEL_STREAM_IDLE_TIMEOUT_MS=60000

# Meta through the LiteLLM gateway (restores prompt caching, see #169 and
# docs/adr/0003-litellm-gateway-for-meta-prompt-caching.md). The gateway is
# separate infrastructure; start the agent with the network overlay:
#   docker compose -f docker-compose.yml -f docker-compose.litellm.yml up -d
# MODEL_API_KEY is the gateway's LITELLM_MASTER_KEY. META_API_KEY then lives
# only in the gateway's configuration: remove it from this file.
# MODEL_BASE_URL=http://litellm:4000
# MODEL_API_KEY=<LITELLM_MASTER_KEY>
# MODEL_AUTH_MODE=auth_token and MODEL_NAME stay at their defaults.
# Name of the external Docker network shared with the gateway (overlay only):
# LITELLM_NETWORK=main

# Alternative backend for testing (Anthropic API directly):
# MODEL_BASE_URL=
# MODEL_AUTH_MODE=api_key
# MODEL_API_KEY=sk-ant-...
# MODEL_NAME=claude-sonnet-5-5
